# FrontRooms map contract: furnish rooms a few ms per frame (office-dress-hitch, visual chat -> map chat)
#
# Owner: the map chat applies this. The visual chat never edits FrontRoomsMapWorld.cs.
# Base:   Assets/Scripts/FrontRoomsMap/FrontRoomsMapWorld.cs as in main on 2026-10-07 (HEAD 16f520e; unchanged at a5262fb6 and ee5c9bb),
#         sha1 9abacc6f11fcc4bf750664ca10a9c173165634b4.
# Result: sha1 6b76a00c9228d7682efb7e3272cfa59dad5ad373.
# History: the same changes were tested on 2026-10-04 against main d610d3a (base 3a3281ad, result 5b597571).
#   They were rebased on 2026-10-07 onto main's newer MapWorld (PassageRevision / TouchPassageRevision,
#   OpeningCostBetween). Only the field block moved, to sit after dressQueue and before TouchPassageRevision();
#   the added/removed lines are identical to the tested patch.
# Precondition: the visual chat's dresser merge is in main: Assets/Scripts/Office/FrontRoomsDressJob.cs and the new
#   FrontRoomsOfficeKit / FrontRoomsFurniturePile / FrontRoomsKitLibrary. The patch casts to FrontRoomsDressJob,
#   so it does not compile without them.
# Apply from the project root:  patch -p1 < Documentation/research/dress_hitch/map_contract/FrontRoomsMapWorld.dress_step.patch
#   (or git apply). Both tools ignore these comment lines.
#
# What it changes (MapWorld only):
#   - ResolveDressers also binds FrontRoomsOfficeKit.BeginDress (6 args) and FrontRoomsFurniturePile.BeginBuild (5 args).
#   - Dress() starts a job (currentJob) instead of the one-frame call. DressNext steps the open job by
#     dressBudgetMs before it dequeues the next room, so only one job is open at a time and the next room's
#     PlaceProps waits. Each chunk's child order stays exactly as it is today.
#   - StepRoom: Cancel when the chunk was dropped or rebuilt; Complete when all=true; Cancel + warning on an exception.
#   - RebuildChunk and Begin(buildAllNow) call DressNext(all: true): they finish at once, because nobody is watching.
#   - ReadyAround and Settled also wait for the open job.
#   - Budget 3 ms on desktop and in the Editor; 2 ms only under #if UNITY_WEBGL && !UNITY_EDITOR (Red's WebGL rule).
#   - Prewarm calls FrontRoomsDressJob.WarmUp(): FrontRoomsKitLibrary.Prewarm plus one off-screen run of both dressers.
#
# Proof that it builds the same map: FrontRoomsDressMapStepTest.cs (next to this file; suggested target
#   Assets/Editor/FrontRoomsMap/; keep its .meta GUID a9b77e1a91c474764b97b11d1d90c64d).
#   -executeMethod FrontRoomsDressMapStepTest.RunBaseline -mapStepOut base.txt -mapStepBaseline <dir>   (before the patch)
#   -executeMethod FrontRoomsDressMapStepTest.RunBatch    -mapStepOut step.txt -mapStepBaseline <dir>   (after the patch)
#   It builds 7 maps. Each one stepped at 3 ms, stepped at 0 ms and built with Complete must equal the
#   one-room-per-frame build, object for object.
#   2026-10-07 re-run in the visual chat's merge clones against this base (attempts 2 and 3): see ../40_merged.md §3 (C_mapstep).
#
# Measured 2026-10-04 (seed 20388, chunk (16,10) room 1, the hitch room): the original dressers took 34.8 ms in one frame.
#   The new dressers without this patch still build it in one frame: ~15 ms on a quiet machine, up to 78 ms under load.
#   With this patch it is a 1.8 ms step: 2 frames at 3 ms, worst step 3.0-3.3 ms.
#
